Z||000000||fldevel||05-26-2000||03:27 PM||||does  anyone know how to safely remove the GT quarter panels off an 85 GT  i have some new ones and was wondaring the safest way to replace them<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-26-2000||04:45 PM||||The windows are held in place with two sided sticky tape.  At one time there was a "fish line" under the window.  If you could get at it you could pull it around the window and it would separate the sail panel from the tape.  Of course the fish line would fall out and hang down and I trimmed mine off.<P>If you still have the fish line, you may be able to separate the sail panel from the tape.  <P>I went to the dealer an paid a few bucks and had him do the replacement.||||reg||3
Z||000002||fieroshop||05-26-2000||08:47 PM||||Old Lar that is not the fastback model. the proper way of taking thos off is to remove the interior trim piece that goes from floor to top and is where the seatbelt attaches. You must first remove the seat belt holder at the top and then very carefully remove the trim piece. Once removed there is a round hole on the side and if you shine a light into it you will see a size eleven nut that has to be removed before you can take out the quarter windows.||||reg||1
